seline\\\\n   Step 2.1 ‣ `npx create-next-app@latest hoa-website --typescript`\\\\n   Step 2.2 ‣ Add/verify strict options in `tsconfig.json` (\\\\\\\"strict\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"noImplicitAny\\\\\\\", etc.).\\\\n   Step 2.3 ‣ Configure absolute imports alias (`@/` → `./src`).\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n3.  Tailwind CSS Stub\\\\n   Step 3.1 ‣ `npm i -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer`\\\\n   Step 3.2 ‣ `npx tailwindcss init -p`\\\\n   Step 3.3 ‣ Edit `tailwind.config.js` →\\\\n```\\\\ncontent: [\\\\n  \\\\\\\"./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}\\\\\\\"\\\\n]\\\\n```\\\\n   Step 3.4 ‣ Create `src/styles/globals.css` with Tailwind base/components/utilities imports.  Ensure it is imported in `_app.tsx`.\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n4.  Firebase Project & Secrets\\\\n   Step 4.1 ‣ In GCP console create project **hoa-website-prod**.  \\\\n   Step 4.2 ‣ Enable Firebase, then products: Authentication (Email/Password), Firestore (production mode).  \\\\n   Step 4.3 ‣ Create **service account** “nextjs-server” → role `Firebase Admin` → generate key JSON.  \\\\n   Step 4.4 ‣ Map creds to env-vars:\\\\n```\\\\n# Public (ok to expose in browser)\\\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=\\\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=\\\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=\\\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=\\\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=\\\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=\\\\n# Private – only server & CI\\\\nFIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=\\\\\\\"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\\\\\\\n...\\\\\\\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\nFIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=\\\\n```\\\\n   Step 4.5 ‣ Create `.env.example` containing above keys for onboarding.\\\\n   Step 4.6 ‣ Add helper `src/lib/firebase.ts` to initialize Admin SDK server-side and Client SDK browser-side using env vars.\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n5.  Vercel Project Provisioning\\\\n   Step 5.1 ‣ Org (or personal) Vercel account → **New Project** → import GitHub **hoa-website**.  \\\\n   Step 5.2 ‣ Framework auto-detected = Next.js.  \\\\n   Step 5.3 ‣ Link Environment Variables (above) for **Production**, **Preview**, **Development** scopes.  \\\\n   Step 5.4 ‣ Set “Production Branch” = `main`; build command default `npm run build`; output dir `.next` (default).  \\\\n   Step 5.5 ‣ Generate Vercel **Project Token** (for CI). Store in GitHub Actions secret `VERCEL_TOKEN`.\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n6.  CI/CD Outline (GitHub Actions → Vercel)\\\\n   File: `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`\\\\n```\\\\nname: CI\\\\non:\\\\n  push:\\\\n    branches: [main, develop]\\\\n  pull_request:\\\\njobs:\\\\n  build-and-deploy:\\\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\\\n    steps:\\\\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\\\\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3\\\\n        with:\\\\n          node-version: '18'\\\\n      - run: npm ci\\\\n      - run: npm run lint  # placeholder\\\\n      - run: npm run build\\\\n      - uses: vercel/action@v2\\\\n        with:\\\\n          vercel-token: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}\\\\n          vercel-org-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}\\\\n          vercel-project-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}\\\\n          working-directory: .\\\\n          # Production only on main\\\\n          prod: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}\\\\n```\\\\n   Secrets required: `VERCEL_TOKEN`, `VERCEL_ORG_ID`, `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID`, all added in repo settings.\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n7.  Cross-Team Dependencies & Sequence\\\\n   1) **Infrastructure/DevOps** (this track) completes Steps 1-6 first.  \\\\n   2) **Frontend Feature Teams** can branch off once skeleton & Tailwind are merged.  \\\\n   3) **Backend/Rules Team** defines Firestore security rules & seed data after Firebase (Step 4).  \\\\n   4) **QA** hooks once preview deployments are auto-published via CI.\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n8.  Proposed Subordinate Roles (Supervisor-rank)\\\\n   •  Supervisor – DevOps Engineer: implements GitHub Actions, secret injection, branch protection.  \\\\n   •  Supervisor – Firebase Integrator: provisions Firebase project, service accounts, writes `firebase.ts`, sets security rules.  \\\\n   •  Supervisor – Frontend Scaffolder: finalizes Tailwind setup, implements auth context/provider, produces placeholder pages/routes.\\\\n\\\\n(Recruitment not triggered yet; awaiting Chief confirmation.)\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n9.  Determinism Notes\\\\n   •  All steps specify exact CLI commands or UI form fields.  \\\\n   •  Resource IDs (`VERCEL_PROJECT_ID`, etc.) are deterministic outputs captured once and stored as GitHub secrets for consistent builds.  \\\\n   •  Private keys are base-64 or escaped multiline to avoid newline issues.\\\\n\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n10.  Ready for review / next instructions.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###arch-plan-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###arch-next-steps-001###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 5\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Kaelen (5) with sequence ID arch-next-steps-001:\\\\n\\\\n]Your DEP (arch-plan-001) is APPROVED. 1) Recruit the three Supervisor-rank roles you outlined (DevOps Engineer, Firebase Integrator, Front-end Scaffolder) using RECRUIT calls. 2) After recruitment, create a short Execution Sprint-0 plan that lists concrete tasks for each supervisor (one file/agent at a time), any immediate CLI commands, and required secrets. Return via REPORT with sequence ID arch-exec-001.\\\"\\n}\\n###arch-next-steps-001###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1753661523930,"endTime":1753661530241